{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_request_genesis_register", "label": "Request \u2014 the genesis register, entries 1 to the seam", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Register has always begun at 165 because the first events happened in another project; the opening block is requested so the reader sees the whole arc from the beginning."}, {"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_canonical_entry_form", "label": "The canonical entry form \u2014 headline, then italic body", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed density, each entry self-contained, nothing decorative: an entry exists because something rests on it, corrections keep both states and name the entry corrected, measurements carry the number and what it was measured on."}, {"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_seam_anchor_165", "label": "The seam anchor at entry 165", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The requested block runs up to but not including the destination's first entry, so the join is exact and no renumbering is guessed at."}, {"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_subject_matter_only_rule", "label": "Subject matter only \u2014 a hard rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Editorial, production, tooling and reader-audit events never enter the reader-facing register; an entry belongs only if it is part of the theory's derivation as a reader would care about it."}, {"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_do_not_pad_or_trim_to_164", "label": "Report the true count K; do not pad or trim", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing asks the responder to match a target count, because a padded count would make the register's own tally false."}, {"id": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_reserved_cell_recount", "label": "The reserved-cell recount, 78 corrected to 92", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named as an example of a correction that keeps both states: the wrong figure and the figure that put it right both stand."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_request_genesis_register", "target": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_canonical_entry_form", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_seam_anchor_165", "target": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_request_genesis_register", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/REQUEST-genesis-register-1-to-164.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_subject_matter_only_rule", "target": "recovered_request_genesis_register_1_to_164_request_genesis_register", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_